# Storefront relay rules (dropshipping repo)

These rules cover only the `dropshipping` repo. Other repos in this workspace have their own always-on rules (automation-pitch relay, Mantine, Tabler, workflow serialization, visual-improvement log); none of those apply here.

This repo is built by sequential slice agents. You are one of them. Work only on the slice named in your kickoff prompt. The user reviews after the whole relay, not after each slice.

## Before changing anything

1. Read `.docs/GOAL.md` (frozen clauses), `.docs/BUILD_PLAN.md` (protocol in Section 4, your slice in Section 5), every entry in `.docs/handoff.md`, this rule, and `public-repo-hygiene.mdc`. Read `.docs/BUSINESS_NOTES.md` when your slice touches pricing, compliance, vendors, payments, or customer emails.
2. `git status` must be clean and `git log -1` must match the COMPLETE commit recorded for the previous slice in `handoff.md`. If not, stop and report. Slice 0 instead checks the baseline facts in BUILD_PLAN Section 0.
3. From Slice 1 on, `npm install`, `npm run build`, `npm run test:unit`, and `npm run leak-check` must be green before you start.

## Scope and contract

- Implement your slice only. Something worth doing outside it is a note for a later slice, not a change.
- A defect in an earlier slice may be fixed minimally when it blocks you; record it in your handoff entry.
- `.docs/GOAL.md` clauses are never edited. If the contract is ambiguous, or you need a new dependency or a product decision, stop and ask the user. Approved changes go under `## Amendments` in GOAL.md, dated, citing clause IDs.
- The approved stack is BUILD_PLAN Section 2 ("Stack and approved libraries"). No other runtime dependency without asking.
- Money is integer cents plus a currency code; only the server computes prices.
- No personal-WeChat bots, marketplace scraping, or unattended purchases on third-party sites (OF-04).

## Finishing a slice

1. Run `npm run build`, `npm run test:unit`, `npm run leak-check`, and `npm run test:e2e` when any browser flow changed (the full suite in Slices 1, 4, 5, 6, and 11). Report exact results.
2. Save review screenshots under `.docs/evidence/NN-<slug>/` as PNG at 390x844 and 1440x900, demo brands only.
3. Append one entry to `.docs/handoff.md` using its template, with `Status: COMPLETE` and the intended commit subject. Never rewrite earlier entries.
4. Commit as `feat(slice-NN): <short title>` (Slice 0: `chore: establish storefront baseline`). Do not wait for review. Never push, branch, deploy, or run another slice.
5. Confirm a clean tree. In the final message, report the commit hash, test results, evidence paths, and that the user can start Slice N+1 in a fresh chat from this HEAD.
